***

### SYSTEM AND METHOD FOR CONTROL OF A HEARING AID DEVICE VIA AN INTEGRATED MEMORY CARD RADIO INTERFACE

#### FIELD OF THE INVENTION
The present disclosure generally relates to wireless hearing device control systems, and more particularly to a system and method for controlling a hearing aid via a radio transceiver integrated within a Secure Digital (SD) card operatively coupled to a mobile user device.

#### SUMMARY OF THE INVENTION
In accordance with one aspect of the present disclosure, a system for wirelessly controlling a hearing aid is provided. Said system comprises:
*   a mobile user device comprising a primary processor, a memory card slot, and a graphical user interface;
*   a software application stored on said mobile user device and executable by said primary processor;
*   a Secure Digital (SD) card configured to be removably inserted into said memory card slot of said mobile user device, wherein said SD card comprises an integrated radio transceiver and a local card controller coupled to said radio transceiver; and
*   a hearing aid device comprising a wireless receiving interface and a signal processing unit.

In one embodiment, said software application is configured to generate a hearing aid control instruction in response to a user input received via said graphical user interface. Said mobile user device is configured to transmit said hearing aid control instruction to said SD card via a host controller interface of said memory card slot. Said local card controller of said SD card is configured to receive said hearing aid control instruction, format said instruction into a radio frequency (RF) protocol payload, and cause said integrated radio transceiver to wirelessly transmit an RF control signal to said hearing aid device, thereby altering an operational parameter of said hearing aid device.

In accordance with another aspect of the present disclosure, a method for controlling a hearing aid is provided, **said method comprising**:
*   detecting, via a software application executing on a mobile user device, a user interaction corresponding to a requested adjustment of a hearing aid parameter;
*   generating, by said software application, a command packet corresponding to said requested adjustment;
*   communicating said command packet from said mobile user device to an SD card disposed within a card interface slot of **said mobile user device**;
*   processing, by a dedicated memory controller within said SD card, said command packet to drive an integrated wireless radio transceiver housed within said SD card;
*   emitting, via said integrated wireless radio transceiver of said SD card, a wireless signal carrying said requested adjustment;
*   receiving, by a wireless receiver of said hearing aid, said wireless signal; and
*   adjusting, by a digital signal processor of said hearing aid, at least one acoustic amplification parameter of said hearing aid in accordance with said wireless signal.

Wherein, in a preferred embodiment, said communicating said command packet from said mobile user device to said SD card comprises writing data to a predetermined physical memory address of said SD card, wherein said dedicated memory controller is configured to interpret writes to said predetermined physical memory address as commands for controlling said integrated wireless radio transceiver.

Wherein, in another embodiment, said at least one acoustic amplification parameter is selected from a group consisting of: master volume level, frequency response profile, directional microphone sensitivity, background noise reduction threshold, and power management state.
